{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-content-scaling-correspondence","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:content-scaling-correspondence","kind":"proposition","title":"Box content is the $q$-Jucys--Murphy eigenvalue exponent","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-knot-eigenbasis-complete","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hecke-algebra-from-braiding"],"cites":["references/jimbo1986","references/ram1997"],"tags":["schur-weyl","content","magnetic-quantum-number","scaling","braid-graph"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.seminormalRep_qJM","text":"content-scaling-correspondence.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:content-scaling-correspondence\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Box content is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Jucys--Murphy eigenvalue exponent</em></p>\n<p><em>Under <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Schur--Weyl duality <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"jimbo1986\">[jimbo1986]</span> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V^{\\otimes n} \\cong \\bigoplus_\\lambda V_\\lambda \\otimes S_\\lambda</code>,\nlet <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> be a standard tableau of shape <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\vdash n</code> and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c = j - i</code> be the content\nof the box of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> at position <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(i,j)</code> holding the value <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code>. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c</code> is the eigenvalue exponent\nof the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Jucys--Murphy element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_k</code> on the seminormal basis vector <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v_T</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_\\lambda</code> <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"ram1997\">[ram1997]</span>:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  L_k\\, v_T = q^{2c}\\, v_T .</code></pre>\n<p><em>The content of a box is therefore a total-spin datum of the sub-tower\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V^{\\otimes k} \\subset V^{\\otimes n}</code>, read off along the growth of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code>; it is not a\nweight of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_\\lambda</code>.</em></p>\n"}
